---
// src/pages/404.astro — the "page not found" page.
//
// WHY THIS IS AN .astro FILE AND NOT src/content/docs/404.md
//   Starlight injects its own /404 route and reads a docs entry called `404`
//   for its content. Authoring that page as `docs/404.md` therefore produces
//   two routes for /404 — the injected one and the catch-all `/[...slug]` — and
//   Astro warns that one of them cannot be rendered. `disable404Route: true`
//   in astro.config.mjs turns the injected route off, and this file becomes the
//   single owner of /404. One route, no warning.
//
// The same reasoning keeps this page out of the sidebar: a 404 link in the
// navigation would be a link that is always a dead end.
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';

Astro.response.headers.set('X-Robots-Tag', 'noindex');
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Page not found' }}>
  <p>
    That URL does not exist on docs.cafaye.com. Pages move while cafaye is in
    early development, and this site is new enough that some pages are still
    being written.
  </p>
  <p>Try one of these instead:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/">Home</a> — what cafaye is, and the services table.</li>
    <li><a href="/getting-started/">Getting started</a> — the CLI, and what exists today.</li>
    <li><a href="/services/">Services</a> — one page per service.</li>
    <li><a href="/contracts/">Contracts</a> — how the services find each other.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If a link on this site sent you here, that is a bug worth reporting in
    <a href="https://github.com/cafaye/docs/issues">github.com/cafaye/docs</a>.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>